g&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Arctic–Alpine Botanic Garden","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":69.6768,"lo":18.9763,"d":3154,"ds":"The Arctic–Alpine Botanic Garden (Arktisk alpin Botanisk hage) is the world's northernmost botanic garden. It is located in Tromsø, Norway, and is run by the Tromsø University Museum. It opened in 1994.","wpu":"Arctic–Alpine Botanic Garden","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Botanicgardentromso.jpg/960px-Botanicgardentromso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Grønnåsen Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":69.679316,"lo":18.960725,"d":3371,"ds":"Grønnåsen Church (Norwegian: Grønnåsen kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Tromsø Municipality in Troms county, Norway. It is located in the Breivika area in the northern part of the city of Tromsø on the island of Tromsøya. It is the church for the Grønnåsen parish which is part of the Tromsø domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Nord-Hålogaland.","wpu":"Grønnåsen Church","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d9/Gr%C3%B8nn%C3%A5sen_kirke.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Kroken Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":69.680809,"lo":19.062876,"d":5321,"ds":"Kroken Church (Norwegian: Kroken kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Tromsø Municipality in Troms county, Norway. It is located the Kroken borough in the city of Tromsø. It is the church for the Kroken parish which is part of the Tromsø domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Nord-Hålogaland.","wpu":"Kroken Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Kroken_Church_%282014%29.jpg/960px-Kroken_Church_%282014%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Håkøya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":69.6544,"lo":18.793,"d":6484,"ds":"Håkøya (Norwegian) or Ávká (Northern Sami) is an island in Tromsø Municipality in Troms county, Norway. The 3.69-square-kilometre (1.42 sq mi) island is located in the Sandnessundet strait between the islands Kvaløya and Tromsøya. It is southeast of the village of Eidkjosen on Kvaløya and west of the city of Tromsø on Tromsøya.","wpu":"Håkøya","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Haakoeya_-_Aerial_-_2022.jpg/960px-Haakoeya_-_Aerial_-_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kvaløy Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":69.680601,"lo":18.744188,"d":9049,"ds":"Kvaløy Church (Norwegian: Kvaløy kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Tromsø Municipality in Troms county, Norway. It is located in the village of Kaldfjord on the island of Kvaløya. It is the church for the Kvaløy parish which is part of the Tromsø domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Nord-Hålogaland.","wpu":"Kvaløy Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Kval%C3%B8y_church.JPG/960px-Kval%C3%B8y_church.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Tromsø is a city in Tromsø Municipality in Troms county, Norway. The city is the administrative centre of the municipality and the county. The city is located on the island of Tromsøya which sits in the Tromsøysundet strait, just off the mainland of Northern Norway.","wpu":"Tromsø","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Troms%C3%B8_sentrum_%285835702754%29.jpg/960px-Troms%C3%B8_sentrum_%285835702754%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}